From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:57:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The TrimUI Brick's power key turns it on with a tap (128 ms)
 where it took a 1 s hold, as TrimUI left it (AXP717 register 0x26, 0x1e ->
 0x1c; long press 1.5 s and forced power-off at 10 s kept). Set in SPL with
 the Brick's other PMIC values at every boot, as the PMIC holds it for the
 next power-on while the battery is connected; tried from Linux first, a tap
 started it

---
 board/sunxi/board.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
index 62204d15..496f0150 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -605,6 +605,13 @@ void sunxi_board_init(void)
 		};
 		for (int i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(brick_ldo); i++)
 			pmic_bus_write(brick_ldo[i][0], brick_ldo[i][1]);
+		/*
+		 * The power key: on with a tap (128 ms) where it took a 1 s hold,
+		 * as TrimUI left it (0x1e); long press 1.5 s and forced off at
+		 * 10 s kept. The PMIC holds this while the battery is connected,
+		 * so it is set here at every boot for the next power-on.
+		 */
+		pmic_bus_write(0x26, 0x1c);
 	}
 #endif
 
